Field Type Meaning <code>command</code> string The command as it was typed, such as <code>enroll</code>, <code>cmp enroll</code>, <code>cmp genm crl</code> or <code>est enroll</code> <code>ok</code> boolean <code>true</code> when the exit status is 0 <code>exitStatus</code> number The exit status of the process <code>server</code> string The <code>--server</code> URL without any password. Absent when the command does not contact a server or stops before it does <code>profile</code> string The response profile, <code>compatible</code> or <code>strict</code>. Absent when <code>server</code> is absent <code>exchange</code> array One message record per request, response or failure, and per connection of an EST command, in order. Absent when nothing was sent <code>result</code> object The result of the command. Present on success and with some failures <code>error</code> object The error when <code>ok</code> is <code>false</code> <code>faults</code> array One entry per <code>enroll</code> or <code>poll --fault</code> value, in the order of the help text. <code>name</code> is the fault and <code>messages</code> lists the body types it changed, such as <code>certConf</code>. An empty <code>messages</code> means the fault found no message to change. Absent without <code>--fault</code> <code>trustedOnFirstResponse</code> array The certificates a CMP command trusted from its first response or a SCEP command from its GetCACert answer, each with the fields of a certificate in a result, so that <code>sha256</code> can be compared with the fingerprint the CA published. Absent with <code>--ca-cert</code> or <code>--fingerprint</code>, on the EST commands and on <code>poll</code> and <code>scep poll</code>, which keep the trust of the enrollment <code>warnings</code> array of strings Problems that did not fail the command, such as a CRL signature that does not verify or a response that breaks a rule of the <code>compatible</code> profile <p>An enrollment produces a document like this, shortened:</p> <pre><code>{
  "command": "enroll",
  "ok": true,
  "exitStatus": 0,
  "server": "https://ca.example.com/.well-known/cmp",
  "profile": "compatible",
  "exchange": [
    {"kind": "request", "time": "2026-10-13T01:39:22.235769Z", "size": 486, "body": "ir", "protection": "PBMAC1", "sender": "CN=device-42", "transactionId": "95a9cb74b5c4c3cfd5a4040906e3756b", "senderKid": "6465766963652d3432"},
    {"kind": "response", "time": "2026-10-13T01:39:22.240007Z", "elapsedMs": 4.238, "httpStatus": 200, "contentType": "application/pkixcmp", "size": 1481, "body": "ip", "protection": "PBMAC1", "sender": "CN=Example CA", "status": "accepted", "extraCerts": 1},
    {"kind": "request", "body": "certConf"},
    {"kind": "response", "body": "pkiconf"}
  ],
  "result": {
    "status": "accepted",
    "confirmed": true,
    "certificate": {"subject": "CN=device-42", "issuer": "CN=Example CA", "serial": "EE460F82A9CD474DAED4950B232DC3B8", "notBefore": "2026-10-13T01:38:22Z", "notAfter": "2027-10-13T01:39:22Z", "key": "ECDSA P-256", "sha256": "a79eb735...", "pem": "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n..."},
    "chain": [{"subject": "CN=Example CA"}],
    "saved": ["device.key", "device.pem"]
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>An EST enrollment records its connection, the request and the response:</p> <pre><code>"exchange": [
  {"kind": "connect", "time": "2026-10-21T13:09:59.716Z", "size": 0, "tls": {"version": "TLS 1.3", "cipherSuite": "TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256", "server": "CN=est.example.com"}},
  {"kind": "request", "time": "2026-10-21T13:09:59.717Z", "size": 334, "method": "POST", "path": "/.well-known/est/simpleenroll", "operation": "simpleenroll", "content": "pkcs10", "subject": "CN=device-42"},
  {"kind": "response", "time": "2026-10-21T13:09:59.719Z", "elapsedMs": 1.9, "httpStatus": 200, "contentType": "application/pkcs7-mime; smime-type=certs-only", "size": 588, "operation": "simpleenroll", "content": "certs-only", "certificates": 1}
]
</code></pre>
